					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Design Notes" "Antenna-feed short-circuit limiter, R1 of Integration manual Figure 33 / Table 26. Table 26 lists 10 Ohm, but the text below it requires 19 Ohm or more when the bias comes from VCC_RF at 3.3 V so the short-circuit current stays under 150 mA; 22 Ohm is the nearest standard value. A short at the connector draws about 3.3 V / (22 + ~0.3 L4 DCR + 1.2 module internal feed) = ~140 mA and burns about 0.43 W here, so Table 26's 0.25 W rating is not enough - hence this 0.5 W anti-surge part. (L4 is the 47 nH LQW18AN47NG00D; verify its DCR at order keeps this under 150 mA.) Active-antenna option only: fit with L4 and C52, do not fit for a passive antenna."
			(at 196.85 76.2 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
